(LST-70 — user-defined things are not in the runtime tag system in v1:
 there is no `is a <thing>` predicate. The rejection is clean and names the
 six builtin nouns. The sibling half of the claim — that a list or map of
 user things is likewise deferred — is rejected just as cleanly, with
 "'origin' holds a whole point, not a value"; that repro is `LST-70b` in
 spirit but cannot share this file, so it is recorded here in the header:

   A thing called point has
     a number called x is 0.

   a point called origin.
   a list called places is [origin].
   -> error: 'origin' holds a whole point, not a value

